<task id="042" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Embed `RegardingResolver` review surface (suggestion + confidence + provenance), "Communications Awaiting Association" view, optional Field Mapping on accept, override-reason feedback signal</title>
    <phase>Wave 4 — Channel-aware Communication Code Page</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001, 002, 040</dependencies>
    <blocks>043</blocks>
    <tags>code-page, pcf</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Embeds the `RegardingResolver` PCF review surface via `PolymorphicResolverService`, adds an auth-scoped Dataverse view, and wires Field Mapping + feedback capture; cross-cuts ADR-024/003/008/015; FULL Step 9.5 gates required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-17</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the **review surface** on the Communication Code Page: embed the existing `RegardingResolver` PCF (via `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields`) pre-filled with the Association Engine's **top suggestion + confidence + provenance rationale**, so a reviewer can **accept in one click** or pick another target. Add a **"Communications Awaiting Association"** Dataverse view filtered to `sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)`, matter-level auth-scoped per ADR-003/008. On accept, optionally run **Field Mapping** to inherit fields from the chosen parent. Capture **override reasons** when the reviewer picks a target other than the top suggestion — persisted as a **feedback signal only** (no learning loop in R4).

    REUSE the existing regarding machinery — do NOT add a new regarding mechanism (spec MUST NOT / Component Justification §11). Extend the `RegardingResolver` catalog if a target is missing; add no new branches.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke front-end + PCF integration engineer. Expert on the regarding family: `RegardingResolver` PCF, `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields`, `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`, `FieldMappingService`. Familiar with Dataverse view authoring and matter-level authorization (ADR-003/008).
  </role>

  <goal>
    The Code Page's review path renders the `RegardingResolver` PCF pre-filled with the engine's top suggestion (target entity + confidence + provenance rationale drawn from `sprk_associationprovenance`). A reviewer confirms in ≤1 click or picks another target; on accept the chosen regarding lookup is written via `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields`, optional Field Mapping inherits parent fields, and any override (non-top-suggestion pick) captures a reason persisted as a feedback signal. A "Communications Awaiting Association" Dataverse view lists `sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)`, matter-level auth-scoped. Build clean via `npm run build:prod`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      W1's Association Engine writes `sprk_associationstatus` + `sprk_associationprovenance` (JSON) + typed regarding lookups. Deterministic ≥0.85 auto-files (status `Resolved`); everything else (`Suggested`/`Pending Review`/`Ambiguous`) needs human review. This task is that review loop's UI — the minimum to close the loop (NOT the full Triage Workbench, which is out of scope / DEC-10).

      AI rungs never auto-file (spec MUST) — they always land as `Suggested`/`Ambiguous`, so they always flow through this review surface. Override reasons are captured as signal only; the feedback-learning loop is explicitly out of scope.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/code-pages/CommunicationPage/src/index.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/FieldMappingService.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-17: reviewer confirms/overrides a suggestion in ≤1 click; view is matter-level auth-scoped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Reuse the regarding family — `RegardingResolver` PCF + `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` + `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`. Keep writing ADR-024 typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT add a new regarding mechanism — extend the existing catalog/map/priority only (Component Justification §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">Review surface + "Communications Awaiting Association" view are matter-level auth-scoped (ADR-003/008); AI flags privilege, never decides it (ADR-015).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Any privilege signal is FLAGGED for the reviewer, never auto-decided by the surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Override reasons persisted as a feedback SIGNAL only — no learning loop in R4 (Out of Scope).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">View filter uses `sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)` — use the option-set integers verified in task 002 (do NOT hardcode unverified integers).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject `authenticatedFetch`; no self-MSAL; PCF consumes host context.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build with `npm run build:prod`; PCF prod build per pcf-deploy conventions; `npm install --legacy-peer-deps`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-privilege-flag-only.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters-authorization.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Regarding resolution via PolymorphicResolverService" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts">
        `applyResolverFields` writes the typed regarding lookup + denormalized fields for the chosen target; feed it the engine's top suggestion pre-fill.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Provenance-driven suggestion pre-fill" location="spec FR-11/FR-17">
        Read `sprk_associationprovenance` JSON → surface target + confidence + rationale next to the resolver for 1-click accept.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Optional Field Mapping on accept" location="docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md">
        On accept, optionally run `FieldMappingService` to inherit fields from the chosen parent (creation-time-style inheritance).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/` and `PolymorphicResolverService.ts` to confirm the embed contract + `applyResolverFields` signature. Read `FieldMappingService.ts` for the optional on-accept mapping call.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the engine's provenance contract (task 001 `sprk_associationprovenance` JSON + `sprk_associationstatus`); confirm how top suggestion + confidence + rationale are represented so the surface can pre-fill.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm the `sprk_associationstatus` integers for `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` verified in task 002 (read task 002 notes / Dataverse MCP) — do NOT hardcode provisional integers.</step>
    <step order="4">Embed the `RegardingResolver` review component into the Code Page (a review slot on top of task 040's shell, shown when `sprk_associationstatus` is a review status). Pre-fill it with the engine top suggestion + confidence + provenance rationale.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement 1-click accept: on confirm, call `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` for the chosen target; set `sprk_associationstatus` → `Resolved`. Implement "pick another" for override.</step>
    <step order="6">Implement override-reason capture: when the accepted target != top suggestion, prompt for a reason and persist it as a feedback signal (a field/note on the record) — signal only, no learning loop.</step>
    <step order="7">Implement optional Field Mapping on accept: offer to inherit parent fields via `FieldMappingService`; make it optional (reviewer opt-in).</step>
    <step order="8">Author the "Communications Awaiting Association" Dataverse view: `sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)`, matter-level auth-scoped (respect ADR-003/008 — do NOT widen visibility). Surface any AI-flagged privilege as a visible flag column (ADR-015), never as an auto-decision.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run build:prod` (Code Page) + PCF prod build if the RegardingResolver bundle changed — confirm clean single artifacts.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-024/015/003/008/§11 reuse). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 042 ✅; confirm 043 unblocked. Update `current-task.md` (record catalog-extension decision if any, feedback-signal storage location; advance).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect RegardingResolver PCF + resolver/field-mapping services</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Embed review surface + accept/override logic</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-deploy">Author the "Communications Awaiting Association" view</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Code Page + PCF prod builds</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor gate</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/code-pages/CommunicationPage/src/index.tsx (UPDATED — review surface embed + accept/override + optional Field Mapping)</output>
    <output type="config">Dataverse "Communications Awaiting Association" view (`sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)`, matter-level auth-scoped)</output>
    <output type="docs">Task notes: catalog-extension decision (if any), override-reason feedback-signal storage, privilege-flag surfacing</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The Code Page renders `RegardingResolver` pre-filled with the engine's top suggestion + confidence + provenance rationale for review-status records.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reviewer accepts a suggestion in ≤1 click; accept writes the typed regarding lookup via `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` and sets status → `Resolved`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reviewer can pick a different target (override); an override captures a reason persisted as a feedback signal (no learning loop invoked).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Optional Field Mapping on accept inherits parent fields via `FieldMappingService` when the reviewer opts in.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Communications Awaiting Association" view exists filtering `sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)` using task-002-verified integers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">View + review surface are matter-level auth-scoped (ADR-003/008); any AI privilege signal is shown as a flag, never auto-decided (ADR-015).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new regarding mechanism added — grep confirms reuse of `PolymorphicResolverService`/`TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` only.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This is the minimum review loop, not the Triage Workbench (DEC-10, out of scope). Keep the surface focused: suggest → accept/override → (optional) map → done.

    Override reasons are a deliberate signal-only capture — the feedback-learning loop is explicitly out of scope for R4. Persist the reason where a future project can consume it, but do NOT build any consumer here.
  </notes>

